  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan with an initial budget of $500,000 for phase one, kicking off on June 15th. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate to leverage AI research. The team has expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, including Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Key milestones include the completion of the testing phase (celebrated on October 10th) and the design phase, leading into the development phase led by Omar Jensen. The project is currently gathering innovative ideas for AI-enhanced data visualization tools (due July 20th) and seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience (due end of November)."
